; The CONSUMER shape the exclusion-propagation rule refuses: a signature naming a dependency type the
; dependency's own WIT recorded as `// unexported:`.
;
; It parses — the name IS in the dependency's extern-interface export — and only the WIT seam knows
; the type has no projection on the other side. A generation-time error quoting the dependency's
; recorded reason is the only honest outcome; a `use` of a name the dependency's package does not
; declare would fail in the consumer's own build with a message about a WIT file nobody wrote.

ledger = [
    m: marker,
]
